=== PART E: forced relations among (kappa, L*, u)
  L* = sigma_c^2/a0                             -> POSIT: A76/A65 premise; D8: not in the action, no tethered-state term; D8b: sigma not one constant
  I(y_t) = 8 pi/kappa^2                         -> POSIT (P5 closure): D7: one-to-one relabelling of kappa; y_t has no independent observable today
  u = f(a0) or f(L*)                            -> NONE in the action: P4 is a posit on the cold sector; no action term carries u (THEORY P4; D6 H-VR is a new posit). The measured u_MID depends on a0 through the inversion (Part C), a measurement coupling, not a relation.
  eta = gamma                                   -> NOT FORCED: A69/A77: action invariant for arbitrary (eta, gamma)
  screening variable s = (8/3) r_h r_M / L*^2   -> FORCED combination (reparametrisation): gamma = K L*^2/2 with saturation scale a0/K: L* enters observables only via L*^2 a0^(1/2) at fixed system; it fixes the degeneracy direction d ln L*/d ln a0 = -1/4 at fixed s, removes no constant, and predicts no new number
  => no relation among kappa, L* and u follows from the action without inserting a number. LEE / second prediction: not applicable.

